      "assessment": "R2 synthesis first returns inconsistent ranked and selected ordering, then repairs it without changing selected tick arrays. It correctly identifies nonmonotonic early outcomes and same-wave differences, but rejects G2 component tests based on the source score, propagates erroneous third-window mechanics, and labels round2 selections final-round advice despite three rounds left. R3 executes the restoration, late trim, early extension and third-window trim with Means 4.123576, 4.123618, 4.075736 and 4.123561.",
      "decision_update": "Preserve the repaired ranking contract and explicit known-schedule status. Assess trial value from its action and expected discrimination, not just ancestor score; verify citations support the claimed mechanism and read remaining budget from host metadata.",
      "counterexample_or_limitation": "The new early extension fails again, while repeated schedules reproduce historical values under shared randomness. This supports conditional nonmonotonicity, not independent replication or a universal optimum. The invalid and repaired synthesis inputs remain part of this session review.",
